1. Cilium leftovers without a reboot (our wish from the k248 round): `Rex::Rancher::Uninstall->check_cilium_residue(clean => 1)` in its own task on the host. It removes the pins in /sys/fs/bpf/cilium, the cil_* cgroup programs (via bpftool if installed, otherwise a warning), /sys/fs/bpf/tc/globals, /run/cilium/cgroupv2 and /run/cilium, then checks again. Anything left dies asking for a reboot, and a host running RKE2/K3s is not touched. A bare line for our own channel: `cilium_residue_cleanup_cmd`. Without clean the refusal stays, but its text now also names this call. Not run live; the bpftool output format is not verified offline. Decide whether OCP offers it (opt-in), and where (destroy / re-bootstrap path).
2. node_ip from the route (our wish from k254): new option `node_ip_from_route => 1` for rancher_deploy_agent/_server, install_agent/_server and preflight_agent/_server. A joining node with no node_ip takes the source address of `ip -o route get` to the join server. An explicit node_ip wins. The first server derives nothing. preflight_* return the derived address as node_ip. Older Rex::Rancher ignore the option silently, so gate on `Rex::Rancher::Distribution->can('node_ip_from_route')`. Decide whether OCP uses it by default for joins on multi-homed hosts (today the operator passes --node_ip).
3. uninstall_cmd / uninstall_node are now ONE command, `/bin/sh -c '…'`, with single quotes inside. Name and signature are unchanged. Check that OCP never wraps the line in '…' itself. According to the hub, t/29, t/190 and t/50 pass against the new lib (checked read-only).
4. t/190 and t/219 carry a copy of the old refusal text: green, but stale once 0.005 is pinned.

